#{\footnote Hlp_Opening_Data1}
${\footnote Opening Data from a Text File}
K{\footnote Opening Data from a Text File}
+{\footnote Browse:0010}

\ql\li0\fi0\ri100{\f0\fs48\cf1\up0\dn0 Opening Data from a Text File}{
\par}\pard
\ql\li0\fi0\ri100{\f0\fs24\cf0\up0\dn0 Energy Explorer can read data from ASCII text data files.  ASCII data files should contain only numeric }
\ql{\f0\fs24\cf0\up0\dn0 values.  The data file should have the same number of data elements in each row of data.  Each element }
\ql{\f0\fs24\cf0\up0\dn0 should be separated from the following element by one or more spaces.  When a data element is missing or }
\ql{\f0\fs24\cf0\up0\dn0 unavailable, a numeric no-data flag such as -99 should be inserted in its place to ensure that each row of }
\ql{\f0\fs24\cf0\up0\dn0 data has the same number of data elements.  Energy Explorer's default no-data flag is -99, however, any }
\ql{\f0\fs24\cf0\up0\dn0 numeric value can be defined by selecting the menu items Data, Set No-Data Flag.  }{
\par}\pard
\ql\li0\fi0\ri100{\f0\fs24\cf0\up0\dn0
\par}\pard
\ql\li0\fi0\ri100{\f0\fs24\cf0\up0\dn0 The first 19 records in the sample data file DAILY2.DAT are shown in Figure 3.2.  Although DAILY2.DAT }
\ql{\f0\fs24\cf0\up0\dn0 contains daily data", Energy Explorer can also analyze data on yearly, monthly, hourly or sub-hourly }
\ql{\f0\fs24\cf0\up0\dn0 timescales.  }{
\par}\pard
\ql\li0\fi0\ri100{\f0\fs24\cf0\up0\dn0
\par}\pard
\ql\li0\fi0\ri100{\f0\fs24\cf0\up0\dn0    114      10      16      1990       1    61.8   27.23     -99      76}{
\par}\pard
\ql\li0\fi0\ri100{\f0\fs24\cf0\up0\dn0    114      10      17      1990       1    65.2   25.68     -99      79}{
\par}\pard
\ql\li0\fi0\ri100{\f0\fs24\cf0\up0\dn0    114      10      18      1990       1    44.2   35.21     -99      64}{
\par}\pard
\ql\li0\fi0\ri100{\f0\fs24\cf0\up0\dn0    114      10      19      1990       1    42.6   38.66     -99      62}{
\par}\pard
\ql\li0\fi0\ri100{\f0\fs24\cf0\up0\dn0    114      10      20      1990       1    52      32.76     -99      70}{
\par}\pard
\ql\li0\fi0\ri100{\f0\fs24\cf0\up0\dn0    114      10      21      1990       1    44.8   41.29     -99      63}{
\par}\pard
\ql\li0\fi0\ri100{\f0\fs24\cf0\up0\dn0    114      10      22      1990       1    36.8   44.2       -99      57}{
\par}\pard
\ql\li0\fi0\ri100{\f0\fs24\cf0\up0\dn0    114      10      23      1990       1     -99      -99       -99      58}{
\par}\pard
\ql\li0\fi0\ri100{\f0\fs24\cf0\up0\dn0    114      10      24      1990       1    41      39.66     -99      63}{
\par}\pard
\ql\li0\fi0\ri100{\f0\fs24\cf0\up0\dn0    114      10      25      1990       1    41.8   37.66     -99      64}{
\par}\pard
\ql\li0\fi0\ri100{\f0\fs24\cf0\up0\dn0    114      10      26      1990       1    43.2   37.39     -99      62}{
\par}\pard
\ql\li0\fi0\ri100{\f0\fs24\cf0\up0\dn0    114      10      27      1990       1    45.2   33.49     -99      65}{
\par}\pard
\ql\li0\fi0\ri100{\f0\fs24\cf0\up0\dn0    114      10      28      1990       1    46.8   32.49     -99      68}{
\par}\pard
\ql\li0\fi0\ri100{\f0\fs24\cf0\up0\dn0    114      10      29      1990       1    48.4   34.21     -99      68}{
\par}\pard
\ql\li0\fi0\ri100{\f0\fs24\cf0\up0\dn0    114      10      30      1990       1    52.8   33.85     -99      67}{
\par}\pard
\ql\li0\fi0\ri100{\f0\fs24\cf0\up0\dn0    114      10      31      1990       1    55.6   33.31     -99      68}{
